Subject: [PATCH 09747/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-6700: quality scorer
 refuses non-live populations, reports distinct counts

The scorer's docstring opens "Score the world models the live agent actually
emitted". It did not. Its default root held two clones of this repo, so rglob
swept the committed results/ evidence tree once per clone: 1138 of 1248 files
(91%) were that tree, emitted by Qwen3.5-9B, retired 2026-07-28. Two
operator-facing rates were wrong for hours as a result.

find_models now classifies every path first and excludes two classes by
default, each named in the report rather than filtered silently.
nested_repo_clone keys on .git existing, not being a directory, because a
worktree or submodule has .git as a FILE and the two checkouts that caused
this were exactly that shape. committed_results_tree matches "results" as a
whole path part, so my_results_run is not caught. --include-non-live restores
the old population and says the rates are not live rates. An all-excluded
sweep exits non-zero rather than reporting on an empty population.

The report now carries total files, distinct files and distinct goal
predicates, because a duplicated root inflates only the first. The docstring
warns that branch count is size, not quality: the four highest-branch models
(cd82 376, vc33 356, ls20, sp80) transcribe the win grid into literals, which
is the worst memorisation in the corpus.

Measured before shipping. Guarded: 112 models, 93 distinct files, 87 distinct
predicates, 12 degenerate, 25 structural. Opt-in: 1251 / 637 / 504 / 346 /
139. 1139 excluded, all nested_repo_clone -- 1138 committed A/B models plus one
synthetic worktree fixture. Zero live models excluded. The results-tree rule
never fires on this root because both trees sit inside clones, but it is not
decorative: sweeping a clone AS the root classifies the same file
committed_results_tree, since a root's own .git is deliberately not a nested
clone. The two rules cover different sweep shapes.

Mutation-proved: 8 mutations each turn the suite RED (drop the .git check,
weaken it to is_dir, drop the results check, weaken it to a substring, drop
the fail-closed exit, drop the distinct-count line, drop the exclusion
reporting, drop the include-non-live warning). Source restored byte-identical.
13 tests pass; test_suite_mutation_check confirms no tracked file was
rewritten.

The research note gains an append-only addendum reconciling the two reported
rates. Applied together on live distinct predicates (n=87), the executable-
code-only and call-following corrections give 23-39%, best estimate ~30% --
not 2% and not 11%. The 2.0% figure reproduces exactly as a WHOLE-CORPUS
number: 110 of 116 prose-only hits are in the retired-generator tree, 6 are
live. Vocabulary drives the range width (20 predicates) far more than
executable-only (6) or call-following (2), and executable-only has its own
false negatives -- m0r0 is a hand-rolled flood fill whose code names none of
the keywords.

